;; Stone 255.19 — per-locus behaviour lives on the waist. `runner-count` is a DECLARED method of
;; the `(Locus :- [T])` surface, returning `:wat::core::i64`.
;; NEGATIVE: a generic reader claiming the count is a String is refused (ReturnTypeMismatch).
;; This row is what makes the positive `…_18_…_generic_reads_its_count.wat` non-vacuous: a call to
;; an UNDECLARED `:wat::spawn::Locus/<name>` type-checks with a free result (measured: on the
;; pre-stone binary, where the surface had no `runner-count`, this file is accepted, rc=0).
(:wat::core::defn :probe::count :- [T] [l <- (:wat::spawn::Locus :- [T])] -> :wat::core::String
  (:wat::spawn::Locus/runner-count l))
